  "imageName": "arrow.right.to.line",
  "intro": "When an adjective modifies a noun in the dative case (to/for whom?), the adjective must also take dative endings. Masculine and neuter share the same endings: -ому/-ему. Feminine uses -ой/-ей. These endings are similar to prepositional adjective endings but with -у added for masculine/neuter. Remember: adjectives ALWAYS match their noun in gender, number, and case!",
  "rules": [
    "Dative adjectives answer кому? чему? (to whom? to what?) — think of giving, helping, or telling someone.",
    "Key verbs requiring dative: помогать (help), давать (give), звонить (call), писать (write to), говорить (tell).",
    "Feminine dative (-ой/-ей) is identical to genitive, instrumental, and prepositional — context and the noun's ending clarify the case.",
    "The dative masculine ending -ому differs from prepositional -ом by just one letter — watch for this common mix-up."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Я дал книгу новому студенту. (I gave the book to the new student.), masc",
    "Она помогает младшей сестре. (She helps her younger sister.), fem",
    "Мы позвонили старым друзьям. (We called our old friends.), plural",
    "Он рад хорошей погоде. (He is glad for the good weather.), fem"
  ],
